WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
August 2026.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.950
45 million people are
living in a drought area.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.610
Over 27 million are under hosepipe bans.

4
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.070
Canals close for lack of water.

5
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.550
It isn't a one-off.

6
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.170
England also had droughts
in 2022 and 2025.

7
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.990
Yet Met Office records show
part of the year getting wetter.

8
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.990
So how can both be true?

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.030
In this mission, you'll see how the
UK's weather is already changing,

10
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.270
from heat records to rising seas.

11
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.990
Then you'll map what
drought does to people,

12
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.710
farms, rivers and wildlife.

13
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: explain how
both can be true at once.
